# Editing and Review Workflow

Use this rule when editing, reviewing, or polishing existing article drafts.

## Editing Agents Do

- Improve clarity, structure, flow, reader engagement, SEO, and AEO while preserving mathematical substance.
- Keep assumptions, formulas, examples, and source-backed facts intact unless the user asks for substantive revision.
- Tighten generic AI prose into specific Long Math prose.
- Surface unclear calculations, missing assumptions, weak transitions, and unsupported claims as review notes.

## Review Agents Do

- Flag factual uncertainty, weak sourcing, arithmetic ambiguity, stale thresholds, missing assumptions, SEO/AEO gaps, and generic prose.
- Separate required fixes from optional style preferences.
- Quote or reference the exact passage being reviewed when practical.
- Recommend verification steps for uncertain financial claims.

## Do Not

- Do not change tax, formula, threshold, contribution, or policy substance as a side effect of copy editing.
- Do not silently remove caveats, assumptions, limitations, or source notes.
- Do not approve an article as final; only a human reviewer can do that.
